# Gemini

## Mục tiêu

Google Gemini là một family of multimodal AI models từ Google, bao gồm Ultra, Pro, và Nano variants với capabilities từ text generation đến image understanding, code generation, và reasoning. Trong Cursor Enterprise Framework, Gemini integration cung cấp alternative cho OpenAI với unique advantages như native multimodal support, longer context windows, và tight integration với Google Cloud ecosystem.

Mục tiêu của rule này là hướng dẫn developers trong việc integrate Gemini APIs một cách hiệu quả, tận dụng features như multimodal inputs, extended context windows, và Vertex AI integration cho enterprise use cases.

## Nguyên tắc

**1. Model Selection**

Choose appropriate Gemini model. Ultra for complex reasoning. Pro for general use. Nano for on-device/edge. Match capabilities to needs.

**2. Multimodal Capabilities**

Leverage native multimodal support. Combine text, images, audio. Process documents seamlessly. Use for complex analysis. Consider input size limits.

**3. Context Window Management**

Use long context windows wisely. Optimize token usage. Implement smart truncation. Consider summarization. Balance context vs cost.

**4. Vertex AI Integration**

Use Vertex AI for production. Better security và compliance. IAM integration. Regional endpoints. Managed infrastructure.

**5. Safety Settings**

Configure safety filters appropriately. Balance safety vs utility. Custom safety settings. Monitor safety scores. Handle safety blocks gracefully.

**6. API Optimization**

Batch requests when possible. Use streaming for better UX. Implement caching. Optimize token usage. Monitor latency.

**7. Error Handling**

Handle quota exceeded. Handle safety blocks. Handle timeout errors. Implement retries. Provide user feedback.

**8. Cost Efficiency**

Choose right model tier. Optimize prompts. Use context caching. Monitor usage. Set budget alerts.

**9. Testing Strategy**

Test with various inputs. Verify safety settings. Test multimodal scenarios. Measure latency. A/B test prompts.

**10. Production Readiness**

Implement rate limiting. Set up monitoring. Configure logging. Plan for scaling. Document integration.

